e_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107018","id":3572217345,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7U67YB","user":{"login":"MadeScientist","id":190612698,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1yE2g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190612698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist","html_url":"https://github.com/MadeScientist","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-24T18:43:18Z","updated_at":"2025-11-25T02:51:35Z","body":"> I was able to replicate the shown behavior. As far as I can see this is ok as nothing is documented to the contrary. What is your use-case? Would using [get_next_scene_tile_id()](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_tilesetscenescollectionsource.html#class-tilesetscenescollectionsource-method-get-next-scene-tile-id) maybe solve your issue?\n\nSometimes when editing AtlasSource, some misoperations lead me to need to delete the old source and then import the same thing again. At this point, its default generated ID will not be reset to 0. But it's not a big problem, I am now ensuring that I always receive the first source in the list(without worrying about any modifications made during my editing process) by combining the use of get_source_id (0) and get_source(). My original understanding was that if I delete a source with ID 0 and add it again, it should start counting again from 0 (if there is only one source in total). At this point, only using get_ source (0) directly may not be able to obtain the correct source.\n\n<img width=\"1274\" height=\"128\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b76c0d0b-ad9f-4bbe-9783-f62ceeeccc69\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3572217345/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]